  "conclusions": [
    "The activation-tensor mutation path is semantically controlled: writing an all-one mask reproduces exact NLL and top-1 predictions on every scored position.",
    "Naive post-training fixed-group pruning has no useful quality-capacity tier in this smoke. Removing only 6.25% of expert neurons increases relative perplexity by 11.42%; retaining 75% increases it by 32.80%.",
    "This is not a rejection of structured co-training. Only 1314 of 6144 layer/expert pairs have direct calibration observations in the larger sweep, unseen experts use a layer-pooled fallback, no weights are updated, and only 17 held-out positions are scored.",
    "A real co-design attempt must train or distill an unquantized checkpoint with an explicit eight-neuron group penalty, then require an all-domain held-out relative-perplexity delta at or below 1% before implementing a grouped storage kernel."
  ]
